# Footguns: database and SQL

Distilled from [docs/LESSONS_LEARNED.md § Database / SQL gotchas](../../docs/LESSONS_LEARNED.md#database--sql-gotchas); that page is the narrative, this is the checklist. Schema reference: [docs/technical/DB_SCHEMA.md](../../docs/technical/DB_SCHEMA.md).

- **Check `information_schema` before assuming a column.** `image_model_scores.normalized` (not `normalized_score`); `image_phase_status.last_error` / `attempt_count` exist; `file_size`, `error_message`, `ml_phase`, `cull_failed` did **not** exist where assumed.
- **Postgres cannot reference a SELECT alias in `ORDER BY`/`HAVING`** — repeat the expression. POSIX regex has no `\d`; use `[0-9]`.
- **Pooled connections:** `PGConnectionManager.__exit__` must roll back on any non-commit path; for read-only work `set_session(readonly=True)` and restore it in `finally` before release.
- **Phantom scores:** per-model `image_model_scores` rows can exist without `score_general` / `SCORING=DONE` after an interruption, or after a re-index wiped the composite (#830); use `modules/phantom_score_finalize.py`, not the phase-only reconcile.
- **A partial result passed to `upsert_image` blanks the columns it doesn't carry.** Its `ON CONFLICT (file_path) DO UPDATE` sets every listed column from `EXCLUDED`. That has bitten three times: keywords (#347), score, rating and label (#830), and title, description and thumbnails (#861). Before a new caller passes a partial dict, check which columns it would reset, and guard them the way `_keywords_provided` / `_scores_provided` do.
- **Large ruff counts in `db_legacy.py` / `db_postgres.py` are pre-existing debt** — lint your new lines, leave the rest (minimal diff).
